WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.727
Welcome to Module 5 Reasoning with SQL Logic In the
previous

00:00:05.752 --> 00:00:10.780
module we focused on summarizing data In this module
we are going

00:00:10.793 --> 00:00:14.968
to focus on decision making In other words how can
we tell

00:00:14.994 --> 00:00:19.246
SQL exactly which records we want how different
conditions should work together

00:00:19.517 --> 00:00:23.486
and what should happen when information is missing
We will work with

00:00:23.512 --> 00:00:27.958
AND OR and NOT We will also look at TRUE FALSE and

00:00:27.983 --> 00:00:32.056
UNKNOWN because SQL does not always work with only
two logical states

00:00:32.945 --> 00:00:36.489
Later we will use tools such as coalesce null if and
case

00:00:36.514 --> 00:00:41.038
expressions to build more realistic business rules
As you move through this

00:00:41.063 --> 00:00:45.844
module do not just memorize the syntax Try to read
each SQL

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:50.767
condition as a sentence Ask yourself what rule am I
actually giving

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:51.721
to the database
